Look at in the mailbag here. we got a message from Tom Gillard down in Tallahoma, Tennessee,

16
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:35,000
And Tom had this to say. he says, talking about clinkers, I heard one the other day.

17
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:42,000
I overheard a group of Scouts talking and one of them was a little concerned about a merit badge that her son had been working on.

18
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:48,000
She was worried that he hadn't worked on in about a year and wondered if he had to start it all over again

19
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:51,000
or if he could just use the requirements he already had signed off.

20
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:55,000
So I piped up and I said no, once they're signed off, the requirements are good.

21
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:57,000
He can work on them anytime he wants.

22
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:03,000
Then another Scouter said no, no, if any of those requirements are over a year old, he has to do them again.

23
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:07,000
Well, I hadn't ever seen this anywhere And so I questioned him about it.

24
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:09,000
I asked him if it was in the new guide to advancement.

25
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:12,000
He backed down a little bit, said it was a troop policy.

26
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:19,000
Aha, a troop policy because they didn't want to have a whole lot of unfinished merit badges on the books.

27
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:24,000
Oh, that's a clinker. Yeah, you found one, Tom.

28
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:27,000
He turned around, he bit his tongue and he walked away.

29
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:31,000
That's classy. That's classy, Tom. I'm glad you did that.

30
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:35,000
Oh my, Yeah, those clinkers are out there, folks, They're out there.

31
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:37,000
We find them every once in a while.

32
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:42,000
That merit badge one, that one's been around since they've had merit badges. I think

33
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:46,000
There's a lot of urban legends that float around about merit badges,

34
